WEBVTT

00:00:09,230 --> 00:00:17,020
Is there a better time of day to take by supplements?

00:00:17,020 --> 00:00:20,020
Well, that depends on what it is that you're taking.

00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:26,020
So, a better time of day to take your supplements in general,

00:00:26,020 --> 00:00:30,020
is it's better to spread your supplements throughout the day.

00:00:30,020 --> 00:00:35,020
So, let's say you're taking three a day of certain supplements

00:00:35,020 --> 00:00:44,020
for most of those, it would be better if you spread them out throughout the whole day.

00:00:44,020 --> 00:00:50,020
Sometimes, if you're taking, let's say, vitamin C to get a higher dose of vitamin C,

00:00:50,020 --> 00:00:53,020
you watch, take it all at once.

00:00:53,020 --> 00:00:57,020
Remember, if you take a lower dose, vitamin C, let's say 1000 milligrams,

00:00:57,020 --> 00:01:00,020
you're absorbing maybe 500 milligrams of that,

00:01:00,020 --> 00:01:05,020
that's going to be an oxidative therapy.

00:01:05,020 --> 00:01:08,020
That's not always wise for a cancer patient.

00:01:08,020 --> 00:01:12,020
If you're trying to get an oxidative therapy out of your vitamin C,

00:01:12,020 --> 00:01:17,020
then maybe you're taking 5000 milligrams a day, 5 grams a day of vitamin C,

00:01:17,020 --> 00:01:24,020
you'd want to take that all at once so that you absorb an oxidative dose.

00:01:24,020 --> 00:01:31,020
But if you're taking things for just general cancer care,

00:01:31,020 --> 00:01:35,020
general immune stimulants, general anti-inflammatories,

00:01:35,020 --> 00:01:39,020
you take those throughout the day because all your supplements have a half-life.

00:01:39,020 --> 00:01:44,020
So, you will, they will dissipate out of your body quite quickly.

00:01:44,020 --> 00:01:49,020
So, and then taking digestive enzymes in HCl,

00:01:49,020 --> 00:01:51,020
you take those only with a meal, right?

00:01:51,020 --> 00:01:56,020
Before your meal, right with your meal or immediately after your meal.

00:01:56,020 --> 00:02:02,020
If you're taking an oxidative approach to melatonin,

00:02:02,020 --> 00:02:06,020
let's say you're taking high-dose melatonin, you may take that,

00:02:06,020 --> 00:02:11,020
you know, 40 milligrams in the morning and 40 milligrams in the evening.

00:02:11,020 --> 00:02:14,020
So, it depends on the supplement.

00:02:14,020 --> 00:02:20,020
General supplements like general nutrition, general anti-inflammatories,

00:02:20,020 --> 00:02:23,020
you don't want to spread those throughout the day.

00:02:23,020 --> 00:02:27,020
And then fat-soluble supplements, it's a little bit different as well

00:02:27,020 --> 00:02:30,020
because fat-soluble supplements you don't need to scratch through the day.

00:02:30,020 --> 00:02:37,020
They'll store in your body and you can just take them any time during the day.

00:02:37,020 --> 00:02:42,020
Sometimes you could hyperlone on vitamin D, per se,

00:02:42,020 --> 00:02:45,020
and just take it once a week.

00:02:45,020 --> 00:02:50,020
But typically I want people to take their vitamin D three with their other

00:02:50,020 --> 00:02:55,020
fat-soluble vitamins that I tell you to take a lower dose every day.

00:02:55,020 --> 00:02:59,020
So, it depends on the supplement that we're talking about,

00:02:59,020 --> 00:03:02,020
on when the time of the day is better to take it.

00:03:02,020 --> 00:03:05,020
Obviously, if you're trying to take something to try to help you sleep,

00:03:05,020 --> 00:03:08,020
you take it in the evening, you know, so things like that.

00:03:08,020 --> 00:03:14,020
So, it depends on what it is that the supplement that you're trying to do with the supplement.

00:03:14,020 --> 00:03:16,020
So, that's the supplement.

